  "title": "Northbound",
  "intent": {"theme": "a long train journey home", "mood": "tired, tender", "pointOfView": "first person, talking to the person beside them", "hook": "Northbound"},
  "settings": {"genre": {"mode": "set", "value": "pop"}},
  "lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nStation clock is running slow\ncoats still wet from yesterday\nyou count the stops on the window glass\nI count the things I didn't say\n\n[Chorus 1]\nNorthbound, and the night is wide\none more town on the other side\nhold on, we're nearly there\nnorthbound, northbound\n\n[Verse 2]\nPaper cups and a broken seat\nyour head is heavy on my arm\nthe conductor calls a name we know\nand neither of us moves at all\n\n[Chorus 2]\nNorthbound, and the night is wide\none more town on the other side\nhold on, we're nearly there\nnorthbound, northbound",
